Z||000000||SCCA FIERO||07-01-2000||07:27 PM||||I got a virus in my computer a while back and have finally gotten rid of it but it messed up my computer. I bought Norton Internet Security 2000 and found the virus (KaK Worm) and quarantined it, then delelted it.<P>Now my computer only boots in safe mode and my settings are all messed up. My pixle setting will only set to the highest setting and none of my programs will run.<P>Where should I start?||||reg||1
Z||000001||86SE||07-01-2000||07:48 PM||||I'd say Backup your important files, format and re-install.  That would be the easyist, most hasstle free way.||||reg||11
Z||000002||SCCA FIERO||07-01-2000||08:05 PM||||Seems alot of my files have become messed up. I tried to reinstall Norton and I couldn't even do that, it just locks up. I even tried to delete Norton and it wouldn't let me do that because some file is corrupt.<P>86SE,how would I go about doing that? You see, I'm not too good at messing with these computers. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||GT Bastard||07-01-2000||08:17 PM||||Easiest solution... Call Norton or visit <A HREF="http://www.Symantec.com" TARGET=_blank>www.Symantec.com</A>  for the fix.  ||||reg||1
Z||000004||86SE||07-01-2000||10:21 PM||||If Symantec can't help you and you dont have any files that are very important to you, or that cant be erased you can format the hard drive.<P>Restart in DOS &gt; at the command prompt (C:&gt; ) type FORMAT C:<BR>The format will begin, takes a while depending on the size of you hard drive.<P>After its all formatted restart the computer with the Windows Setup Diskette in the floppy drive (if you dont already have one you better make one befor you format).<P>The setup disk is a boot disk and it will ask you if you want to stup up computer with CD-ROM support - select YES<P>Put the Windows 98/95/NT/2000 or whatever version you have in the CD-ROM drive and it should start to install.  The rest is pretty much straight foreward, on-screen instructions.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Cooter||07-02-2000||12:04 AM||||Before you format- find the book for your windows O/S- you will need the product ID number off the certificate of authenticity. If you have lost the book, someone here could probably get you a number to use.||||reg||1
Z||000006||SCCA FIERO||07-02-2000||01:51 AM||||I have all the books and CDs that came with my computer. This is getting really bad. Everytime I reboot my computer it gets worse. Now I see small x's and dots all over the screen.<P>Why do people make these viruses? What the hell is wrong with them? They can't see what happens to my computer when it hits... so what's the point?<P>I may be offline for a while  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000007||dogtired||07-02-2000||02:43 AM||||Never had a virus that Penecillin couldn't clear up till now???   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif"><P>Anyway I will be trying the free cleaner located at:<BR>http:/www.pchell.com/internet/kalworm.shtml<BR>maybe that could help you  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Anyone else know of FREE Virus cleaners or scanners???    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||6
Z||000008||Ozzy||07-03-2000||12:44 AM||||Hey SCCA....<P>I have just had it too...I hope to GOD I did not pass it thru to you.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><P>Dude, I am in Ogden this week. Are you done with your Idaho gig? Maybe we can hook up and I can help you thru your PC woes. I have the 2 Fiero's here in town as well. <P>This little bastard virus can only be contracted thru Outlook Express I'm told. I don't know where the hell I got it but it was a pain in the ass for sure. <P>Did you take note of what the file names are that you deleted? Don't re-format yet!! You probably just deleted a file that windows is looking for on boot up. As ;ong as it boots you are still in reasonable shape.<P>Ozzy||||reg||1
Z||000009||dogtired||07-03-2000||03:12 AM||||I am BEGGing for forgiveness,  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif"> if I infected anyone. <P>Thats not the kind of virus I like to spread   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>I did have the one I mentioned above and went to the web page I noted up there and it cleaned it up very quick<P>What the directions called it was "VBS.KAKWorm" It really didn't kill my system but when I would boot up another box would appear that I had never seen before, titled: <BR>Driver Memory Error <BR>and in the box it says: <BR>Kagou-Anti-Kro$oft says not today!<BR>and had a OK box under that???<P>If you choose the OK it would shut down your computer  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif"> if you choose the X in the upper right corner it wouldn't do anything??? <P>Anyway use that WEB address above! It cleaned me right up.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>And again SORRY SORRY SORRY if I sent it to any of my FIERO FORUM friends  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>Ignorance is no excuse for the RULES  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||6
Z||000010||SCCA FIERO||07-03-2000||06:27 PM||||Hey Ozzy.<P>If I got this from you, I may have to kill you  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>I think I got rid of it. The files that got infected must have been to my video card because I reinstalled an update for it and everything seems to be OK now.<P>However I can't seem to get this Norton antivirus to scan my email. When it's on I can't receive any mail, so I have to turn it off. I spent $60 bucks for this virus scanner and you would think they would include some instructions that us idiots can understand.<P>Dog, I got that same message when I got hit. Then every now and then I would get an error for some KaK file.<P>LOL... Maybe I should wear a condom from now on??<P>No hard feelings an my end you guys... $hit happens.<BR><P>------------------<BR>-Chris <BR>88 Fiero Coupe<BR>V6 Fastback||||reg||1
