Z||000014||batboy||07-03-2000||09:29 PM||||Having a computer virus sucks and is a big hassle, but you usually resolve the problem with an up-to-date antivirus program (like Norton 2000) without resorting to reformatting the harddrive, although, there are cases you just about have to do that. Danger: you need to have a current Windows start-up 3.5 floppy disk with your CD-ROM drivers on it. If you only have a Windows upgrade CD-ROM, you're going to be screwed, unless you have a previous Windows version's disks or CD-ROMs. Make sure you back everything up you want to save, because you will lose everything on your harddrive when you reformat.||||reg||1
Z||000015||Ozzy||07-03-2000||11:53 PM||||Hey SCCA....<P><BR>=======&gt;As Ozzy rolls over the floor repeatedley getting the $hit kicked out of him for infecting his Fiero bretheren!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> &lt;=======<P>I guess you must use Outlook Express. There is a patch available for the security hole in Outlook Express on the microsoft website somewhere. It's free too. <P>I'm staying here for at least another week and may have some time on my hands on the weekend. Only thing is I'm probably going to take the GT to Idaho tomorrow. We are moving there soon.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> I have finally tied down the folks at Level3. I'm going to be working for them as an OSP Engineer covering the network from Seattle to Las Vegas. It's real good bucks & bennies; too good to pass up! I can live anywhere in between so Idaho is cheap and my wifes people are there.<P>What the hell happened to this place?? Provo used to be a quiet little town and cheap to live. Easy to commute etc...obviousley not any more.<P>Anyway, I will call you toward the end of the week. Have a good 4th.<P>Ozzy||||reg||1
